From 965b7d86431ce559c9ad8c70a2d2e63b010b50bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:00:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] kboot: T6050: hand the GPU to Linux behind chosen.m5pro,gpu=1

aurora-silicon/linux's G17 M5 driver (apple,agx-g17s) adopts what iBoot
left for the GPU: both coprocessor images loaded but not started, and
the UAT regions published in /arm-io/sgx. It needs them as six named
memory regions, and its two ASCWrap v6 mailboxes at the coprocessors'
addresses. No m1n1 provides that for T6050 yet ("unsupported chip").

With the payload variable chosen.m5pro,gpu=1, dt_set_gpu_t6050() takes
from the ADT of this boot:
 - ttbs, pagetables, handoff, l2-pagetables: sgx gpu-region,
   gfx-shared-region, gfx-handoff, gfx-shared-l2-region;
 - fw-text: gfx-asc __TEXT start .. gfx1-asc __TEXT end, fw-data:
   gfx-asc __DATA start .. gfx1-asc __DATA_SHARED_RO end, from
   segment-ranges, each required to be contiguous and the DATA bases to
   match the sgx properties (the images moved by 0x8000 between mBoot
   41.x and 60.65, so nothing is hardcoded);
 - for each mailbox the GPU node names, the wrapper and iop-vbar of the
   coprocessor whose ADT role matches its apple,firmware-role.
It checks the GPU node's sgx window, the mailboxes' interrupts and the
PMGR power-state registers of the GPU's power domain node against the
ADT, then sets the regions, the mailboxes,
the GPU node and its PMGR node okay. Any failed check leaves them all
disabled and the boot continues; nothing here fails the boot or writes
a register. It logs the four GPU power-state words.

Without the variable nothing changes: the DT's GPU nodes stay as the DT
has them. kboot_get_chosen(), pmgr_psreg_by_name() and
pmgr_power_is_on() are the helpers of the T6050 N1 hand-off, added here
byte for byte so that the two series merge in either order.

On J716s none of the coprocessors involved has an __OS_LOG segment, and
all six regions lie outside the RAM Linux gets (fw-text/fw-data below
phys_base, the UAT regions above its end).

Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
---
 src/kboot.c     |  12 ++
 src/kboot.h     |   1 +
 src/kboot_gpu.c | 547 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/pmgr.c      |  23 ++
 src/pmgr.h      |   2 +
 5 files changed, 585 insertions(+)

